name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q2_2025'

question 'A developer has an array called `users` that contains exactly 5 names. If they try to display the user at `users[5]`, what will the app likely show?'

wrong 'The name of the 5th user in the list.'
right ' An "undefined" value or an empty space, because that index does not exist.'
wrong ' The name of the 1st user in the list.'
wrong 'A list of all 5 users at once.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

Because arrays are zero-indexed, a list with 5 items uses indexes 0, 1, 2, 3, and 4. Attempting to access index 5 points to a sixth position that hasn't been defined.
MARKDOWN
